# Does the player's Rest ('z', KY_CMD_SLEEP -> EV_REST) now work while
# POISONED, and do the poison's Fort saves roll during that rest? Read by
# tools/check_rest_poison.sh. bd inc-gmrj.
#
# 'z' MUST BE LOWERCASE. KY_CMD_SLEEP is { 'Z', 0 } (src/Tables.cpp:5389) and
# the keyset compares modifier flags exactly, so a shifted 'Z' matches
# nothing (src/KeyScript.cpp:22, and see tools/keys/field-day-duration.keys's
# own header, which hit the same trap first). A literal 'Z' in a key script
# is silently swallowed by no case at all -- confirmed empirically: it left
# every following screen byte-identical to the one before it.
#
# DEPTH 2, NOT 1. Player::Rest refuses depth 1 by design ("you can just climb
# back out of the dungeon entirely") -- again per field-day-duration.keys's
# header. GENOCIDE EVERYTHING first: the rest is separately refused while any
# hostile is in plain sight (Rest's own RestEncounterChance/in_sight check),
# and the Goblin Caves' entry chamber is littered with corpses AND live
# monsters in view. Both steps are the same route field-day-duration.keys
# uses to reach a clean rest.
#
# THE ROUTE. tools/fixtures/rest-poison-god.irh, spliced onto a scratch copy
# of lib/main.irc by the check script (never onto the tracked lib/), declares
# one test god. "Become Divine Champion" (wizard mode) joins it and grants
# 30000 favour outright (src/Debug.cpp), which fires its EV_BLESSING once; the
# handler calls GainPermStati(POISONED,...) with $"arsenic" -- lib/threats.irh
# :389, cval 4 / sval 13 / lval 3. gainedFavour() prints its own level-up
# messages, paginated ("more --") and followed by a scrollable "ESC:Done"
# list -- @while drains both, the same two lines heal-maladies.keys uses for
# the same god-join step.
#
#   CONTROL  wizard "Examine Player Data" dumps the Stati list; it must name
#            POISONED, or the affliction never landed and the check is
#            UNMEASURED.
#   REFUSAL  'z' throws EV_REST. The BEFORE (unfixed) engine refuses at
#            Player::Rest's POISONED guard and prints "You're too busy dying
#            at the moment to think about rest." with NO further prompt (the
#            refusal sits before the REST_DUNGEON confirm block). The fixed
#            engine instead asks "Confirm rest in dungeon? [yn]" -- OPT_
#            SAFEREST is off in tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat, so an
#            in-dungeon rest always asks.
#   WOKE     'y' answers the confirm prompt (meaningful only in the fixed
#            engine; in the unfixed one 'y' lands as an ordinary command key
#            with the refusal already delivered). The two SPACEs drain any
#            "-- more --" pagination from the night's own messages (the
#            poison save line(s), the overcome line, the wake line, the
#            armour line can together run past one screen). A rest that
#            completes prints "You awaken feeling well rested and
#            recovered." (Player.cpp's REST_NOMSG-less wake line).
#   AFTER    the same dump again; POISONED must be gone (three saves overcame
#            arsenic, matching Fortitude at these fixtures' levels against DC
#            13 -- see the fixture's own header) or its save count advanced.
#
# THE SEED is pinned by the check script at 1. Tried 1-4: all four resolve
# the poison and complete the rest with no encounter (Percent 100, full
#144000-turn night); seed 5 stalled the script differently (an @choose that
# found nothing) and was dropped rather than chased -- 1 is kept, not
# special-cased for luck.

@include chargen.keys
@until "HP:" ESC

w y
@choose "Ascend / Descend Depth"
"2" ENTER
@until "HP:" ESC

w
@choose "Genocide Everything"
@until "HP:" ESC

w
@choose "Become Divine Champion"
"Rest Poison Test God" ENTER
@while "more --" SPACE
@while "ESC:Done" ESC

w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*10
@dump:control
ESC

z
@dump:refusal
y
SPACE SPACE
@dump:woke

w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*10
@dump:after
ESC
@quit
